<h1>How Fast Are NFL <em>Quarterbacks</em> Now?</h1>
<div class="hero-meta">
<span class="hero-meta-item">📖 6 min read</span>
<span class="hero-meta-item">⚡ Sprint Speed</span>
<span class="hero-meta-item">🏈 Quarterback</span>
</div>
<p class="hero-intro">
    The quarterback position used to be the one place on the field where speed was optional. That's no longer true. At the 2026 NFL Combine, quarterbacks averaged 4.60 seconds in the 40 — the second-fastest mark for the position ever recorded, and part of a trend that's been building for years.
  </p>
</div><div class="article-wrap">
<div class="content">
<!-- QUICK ANSWER BOX -->
<div class="callout" style="background:var(--surface);border-color:var(--accent);">
<div class="callout-icon">⚡</div>
<div class="callout-text"><strong>Quick answer:</strong> NFL quarterbacks averaged <strong>4.60 seconds</strong> in the 40-yard dash at the 2026 combine — the second-fastest average for the position in combine history. It reflects a broader shift toward drafting and developing more mobile, dual-threat quarterbacks rather than a one-year anomaly.</div>
</div>
<!-- SECTION 1 -->
<h2>A Position That's Getting Faster By Design</h2>
<p>For most of NFL history, quarterback was evaluated almost entirely on arm talent, accuracy, and decision-making — speed was a bonus, not a requirement. That calculus has shifted. Modern NFL offenses lean heavily on designed quarterback runs, zone-read concepts, and the threat of extending plays outside the pocket. Teams now actively recruit and develop quarterbacks who can do both, and the combine numbers are starting to reflect it.</p>
<p>The 4.60-second average at the 2026 combine is the second-fastest on record for the position — not an outright record, but firmly part of a multi-year trend rather than a single standout class skewing the number.</p>
<table class="data-table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Benchmark</th>
<th>40-Yard Dash</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr class="elite"><td>2026 combine QB average</td><td>4.60s</td></tr>
<tr><td>Historical QB average (long-term)</td><td>~4.8–4.9s</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fast QB 40 time (NFL level)</td><td>Under 4.7s</td></tr>
<tr><td>Exceptional QB 40 time (NFL level)</td><td>Under 4.6s</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
